From 42ed961392fc4d3510cdb124232de926e1122613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viswanath Kraleti <viswanath.kraleti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:33:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] workaround: configs: qcom_shikra_spl: give the fit structure
 room for image signatures

The SPL loads the FIT structure at CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS and keeps
reading it while it loads and starts QcLib. At 0x0C2C1800 it has 8 KiB
before qclib_1, which loads at 0x0C2C3800. That is enough for a FIT with
signed configurations, but with SPL_SIGN_INDIVIDUAL the structure grows
to about 12 KiB and loading qclib_1 overwrites its end.

Move it to 0x0C2B1800, right after the ECC blob slot (0x0C2B1400 +
0x400). Nothing else uses 0x0C2B1800-0x0C2C3800, so the structure gets
72 KB, and it stays inside the BOOTIMEM range flushed before QcLib runs.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/u-boot/pull/243]

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Viswanath Kraleti <viswanath.kraleti@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 configs/qcom_shikra_spl_defconfig | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/qcom_shikra_spl_defconfig b/configs/qcom_shikra_spl_defconfig
index 5d1bc5d40fe..9f6cdab0f48 100644
--- a/configs/qcom_shikra_spl_defconfig
+++ b/configs/qcom_shikra_spl_defconfig
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ CONFIG_SPL_ATF=y
 CONFIG_SPL_ATF_LOAD_IMAGE_V2=y
 CONFIG_SPL_ATF_NO_PLATFORM_PARAM=y
 CONFIG_SPL_HAS_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS=y
-CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS=0x0C2C1800
+CONFIG_SPL_LOAD_FIT_ADDRESS=0x0C2B1800
 # CONFIG_SPL_SHARES_INIT_SP_ADDR is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_HAVE_INIT_STACK=y
 CONFIG_SPL_STACK=0x0C294800
@@ -81,4 +81,4 @@ CONFIG_QCOM_DDR_TRAINING_SUPPORTED=y
 CONFIG_QCOM_DDR_TRAINING_USE_PARTITION_NAME=y
 CONFIG_QCOM_DDR_TRAINING_PARTITION_NAME="ddr"
 CONFIG_QCOM_SPL_BOOTIMEM_DDR_TRAINING_BASE=0x0c368000
-CONFIG_QCOM_SPL_BOOTIMEM_DDR_TRAINING_SIZE=0x8000
\ No newline at end of file
+CONFIG_QCOM_SPL_BOOTIMEM_DDR_TRAINING_SIZE=0x8000
